# Resist ward: a 1x1 WARD TOWER with a light crystal floating over it. Placed against a wall, it covers the connected
# wall and gate segments (StructureSystem::rebuildWardLinks): a barrier of light around them takes a share off every hit,
# paid from its light store (Wards.cpp). It takes light like any consumer, at "Refill (light/s)" at most. Spawned origin
# 1.75 above ground; the crystal's centre is Light.cpp's beamHeightOf (2.65 over the origin): keep them in step.
# wardAbsorb.pre and wardRetaliate.pre are the same tower with another colour.
# SHAPE (a placeholder): a full 2 x 2 x 2 m stone block whose flat top is at a Walkway deck's height (2 m), so a ward
# between walkways carries the walk on (the deck solve takes its top as a fixed edge: solveWalkwayDecks). The magic
# stays OFF the walk: a glowing band around the block under the decks' planks (1 cm proud of the faces), a glowing
# rune set flush into the top, and the crystal floating high over it (its lowest point 3.95 m up: a player on the
# top walks under it). The collider is the block alone.
Prefab gameWardResist
	Global true
	Component Render
		ObjectContainer baseshapes
		Node Cube
		Type StaticMesh
		Color 0.5 0.47 0.42
		Position 0 -0.75 0
		Scale 1
	Component Physics
		Body Static
		ContactEvents true
		Shape Box
		HalfExtents 1 1 1
		Offset 0 -0.75 0
	Component GameStructure
		MeleeRadius 1
		AlwaysShowResources true
	Component Scene
		Entity
			Name Band
			Position 0 -0.25 0
			Component Render
				ObjectContainer eyes
				Node CubeQuarter
				Type StaticMesh
				Color 1 0.8 0.4
				Emissive 1.5
				Scale 1.005
		Entity
